<CourseLayout title="Recover the impossible." description="Operation Last Light. Four roles, six areas and the last intact research archive at Meridian Station." eyebrow="THE FINAL MISSION / MERIDIAN" wide>
<section class="callout"><h2>This is your final mission: Operation Last Light.</h2><p>Recover Meridian Station's archive using the skills from all twelve weeks. The demonstration below, <strong>Operation Lamplight</strong>, is a different worked example. Your playable Last Light trial begins beneath it.</p><ol><li><strong>Start or resume.</strong> For a first rehearsal, choose Baseline, select Start new trial and confirm if prompted. Then choose the Declared recovery objective before selecting a role or operating equipment. Saved work resumes automatically with its initial objective locked; start a new trial to choose a different objective.</li><li><strong>Follow the Mission Journal.</strong> Go to each objective, read its instruction and use the relevant role's controls. Solo practice lets you switch roles; teams share one browser and rotate control.</li><li><strong>Preserve the plan and a revision.</strong> The coordinator records versions at Dispatch. Keep the original when evidence changes.</li><li><strong>Finish and keep the record.</strong> Complete the required objectives, choose a justified resolution at Dispatch, read the debrief and export. Write the team explanation after playing.</li></ol><p><a href={withBase("/assessments/final-project/")}>Read the full final-project steps and submission checklist →</a></p></section>
<DemonstrationLink id="assessment-final"/>
<Mission kind="recovery"/>
</CourseLayout>
